      "status_notes": "CVE-2025-12781: base64.b64decode(), standard_b64decode() and urlsafe_b64decode() always accept the '+' and '/' characters, even when altchars selects a different alphabet, which can let differently encoded data pass a check. Upstream addressed it on the main branch, in issue https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/125346 and commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/9060b4abbe475591b6230b23c2afefeff26fcca5, by emitting a warning (a DeprecationWarning or a FutureWarning) for such input, a change listed in the CPython 3.15 What's New; the 3.13 and 3.14 commits linked from the CVE record add tests only, and no CPython 3.10 release carries the change. See https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-12781. Checked Lib/base64.py in the python-3.10 package of every build published in the DHI Alpine 3.23 repository, 3.10.19-r0 to 3.10.22-r8, x86_64 and aarch64; both architectures agree. Every published build ships the upstream 3.10 base64.py, which has no such check, so every published build is affected."
    },
